# Docker matches these patterns from the context root only, so anything that can also appear inside a workspace package
# (apps/*, packages/*) needs a `**/` prefix. Without it the host's nested `node_modules` and `dist` are copied over the
# image's own install and build, and host-only caches and secrets leak into the image.
**/node_modules
.git
**/.tandem
**/*.log
**/dist
**/.env*
compose.override.*
docker-compose.override.*
**/.DS_Store
